s and museums across  the city  consequences to health and not doing it  are really bad  it's just been so overwhelming the virus  continues to rip families apart  bonnie surya nahara of el paso lost six  family members to covet 19  including both her parents not even an  hour had passed when they tell me  your mother just passed away when i get  a call and say we're about to put your  dad on a ventilator  nahara also lost an uncle two aunts and  a cousin  she says watching her mother celebrate  her final birthday a year ago  is bittersweet i love seeing the videos  because i love seeing her face  it makes me so mad that i'm never  gonna have the opportunity that our kids  that our family is never gonna have the  opportunity  to have another birthday celebration  there are some disturbing numbers out  from the american academy of pediatrics  they say more than one million u.s  children have tested positive to date  that's one in every 11 cases since the  start of the pandemic and something else  to consider  students are going to be coming home for  the upcoming holiday season and the cdc  says  while younger people and children tend  to recover faster  they can also spread the disease much  quicker  tony it's definitely a concern omar  thank you very much
 

